  "answer": "Changes made (only the five writable files):\n\n- **`normalize.mjs`**: `normalizeIssue` now builds a fresh object `{ id, title, tags, assignee }` in that order without mutating input. ID/title trimmed (case preserved); tags trimmed, lowercased, empties dropped, first-occurrence de-duplicated into a new array; assignee trimmed/lowercased with empty → `null`, input `null` stays `null`. Validation still via `assertIssue` (`TypeError('invalid issue')`).\n- **`consumers/list.mjs`**: no longer sorts or mutates the input; maps to normalized issues preserving input order (duplicates kept).\n- **`consumers/search.mjs`**: validates query string, uses `listIssues`, trims/lowercases query, empty query returns whole normalized list, otherwise substring match on normalized title or any tag, in original order.\n- **`consumers/activity.mjs`**: uses `listIssues`; renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags.\n- **`serialize.mjs`**: serializes `listIssues(issues)` so order and property order match the list view.\n\nUntouched: `legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, `validators.mjs`, fixtures, and date/paging/console helpers. No tests were executed (no shell available); correctness was checked by reading the code against the stated contract and the example in `public.test.mjs`.",
